            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.1.44</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[## Mose 0.1.44

**Improved**
- A new welcome on first launch: what Mose can do, then the two permissions it needs, then straight into the app. macOS no longer asks for Input Monitoring before Mose has said why.
- Allowing a permission is easier: System Settings opens at the right list, with Mose's icon beside it to drag in. This works everywhere Mose asks, not just on first launch.
- Settings › Buttons shows Input Monitoring next to Accessibility, so you can see and change both in one place.

Requires macOS 15 or later. Ports, cables and displays need a Mac with Apple silicon.
]]></description>
